# ESLint config is dev-only (wp-scripts lint-js reads it locally/in CI; nothing
# at runtime loads it). Shipping it trips WP.org Plugin Check's hidden_files
# check (a dotfile in the release ZIP) -- see task-15-report.md's "Concerns"
# section, where adding .eslintrc.json (Görev 15) first put it in the ZIP.
#
# 2026-09-01: the SAME class recurred. Adding .eslintrc.src-react.js for gate
# G-F put a second dev config in the ZIP, and check-shipped-surface caught it
# (pinned=588 actual=589). One filename per config is a list that goes stale the
# next time someone adds one, so the entry is now a PATTERN: every ESLint config
# at the plugin root is dev-only, without exception.
.eslintrc*

# Website static exports
website/
website/**

# Language artifacts
languages/*-backup-*.pot~
languages/*-backup-*.po~
# msgmerge default backup (no `-backup-` prefix) — the original patterns
# above only matched explicitly-named backup files; default `msgmerge --update`
# without `--backup=none` produces `<slug>-tr_TR.po~` next to the .po, which
# slipped past the patterns into v4.30.2 ZIP. Catch any *.po~ / *.pot~.
languages/*.po~
languages/*.pot~
languages/*-backup-*.l10n.php
# Build-time input for `wp i18n make-json --use-map`, regenerated by
# bin/build-i18n.py on every run. Never read at runtime.
.i18n-map.json

# Temp
# Named files first, then the class: a scratch file that matched neither
# (dead-catalogs.tmp) shipped inside the 5.2.1 and 5.2.2 release ZIPs.
.tmp_scan.csv
.tmp_phpscan.csv
*.tmp
*.log
*.zip
build_debug.txt


# Test artefacts, not build output. build/ ships (the compiled admin bundles
# live there), so anything else dropped into it ships too -- measured: a stray
# phpunit --log-junit file took the shipped surface from 588 to 589 without a
# single gate objecting.
/build/logs/
.claude
